From: ubuntu24-rk <claude@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: hub: disable autosuspend for WCH CH334R

The HZ-RK3506SP MiniEVM carries a WCH CH334R (1a86:8091) four-port hub
on the dwc2 otg1 controller. With runtime autosuspend enabled the hub
loses downstream hotplug: a device plugged into one of its ports gets
VBUS (the rail is always on) but is never enumerated by the host. An
Android phone therefore shows only "charging" and never offers the USB
mode dialog, because its gadget never sees CONNECTED; a USB flash drive
simply does not appear.

hub_probe() forces the autosuspend delay to 0 for hubs, so the CH334R
suspends as soon as it is idle. Over a 22 h uptime it spent 66346 s
suspended against 12931 s active. The connect event stays pending inside
the hub until something resumes it: reading
/sys/bus/usb/devices/2-1:1.0/2-1-portN/disable calls
usb_autopm_get_interface() (drivers/usb/core/port.c), and the device
enumerates at that exact instant. Writing "on" to the hub's
power/control makes hotplug work first time, every time, after which
rndis_host binds and usb0 gets a DHCP lease.

The two guards in autosuspend_check() (drivers/usb/core/driver.c) that
should have prevented this both pass: the CH334R advertises remote wakeup
(bmAttributes 0xe0) so device_can_wakeup() is true, and dwc2 never sets
hcd->cant_recv_wakeups, so the root-hub-child check does not fire either.

Use the existing HUB_QUIRK_DISABLE_AUTOSUSPEND, already applied to the
SMSC USB5534B, Cypress CY7C65632 and TI TUSB8041 hubs for the same class
of problem. This keeps the quirk scoped to the one chip; every other
USB device still autosuspends normally.

Signed-off-by: ubuntu24-rk <claude@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/core/hub.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/usb/core/hub.c	2026-11-08 19:01:57.418702434 +0800
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/hub.c	2026-11-08 19:01:57.434703120 +0800
@@ -55,6 +55,8 @@
 #define USB_PRODUCT_USB4913			0x4913
 #define USB_PRODUCT_USB4914			0x4914
 #define USB_PRODUCT_USB4915			0x4915
+#define USB_VENDOR_WCH			0x1a86
+#define USB_PRODUCT_CH334R		0x8091
 #define HUB_QUIRK_CHECK_PORT_AUTOSUSPEND	BIT(0)
 #define HUB_QUIRK_DISABLE_AUTOSUSPEND		BIT(1)
 #define HUB_QUIRK_REDUCE_FRAME_INTR_BINTERVAL	BIT(2)
@@ -6007,6 +6009,11 @@
       .bInterfaceClass = USB_CLASS_HUB,
       .driver_info = HUB_QUIRK_DISABLE_AUTOSUSPEND},
     { .match_flags = USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_VENDOR
+			| USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_PRODUCT,
+      .idVendor = USB_VENDOR_WCH,
+      .idProduct = USB_PRODUCT_CH334R,
+      .driver_info = HUB_QUIRK_DISABLE_AUTOSUSPEND},
+    { .match_flags = USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_VENDOR
                    | USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_PRODUCT,
       .idVendor = USB_VENDOR_CYPRESS,
       .idProduct = USB_PRODUCT_CY7C65632,
